message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Operator-Specific Forgetting in Matrix-Valued Associative Memory (code and data)"
abstract: >-
  Controlled study of selective forgetting in matrix-valued associative
  memories. Four closed-form residual laws with zero free parameters describe
  the post-erase residual under key/state drift for the complex (phasor) and
  real read channels, verified on trained models at d=64 and d=128 with
  matched load c=(n-1)/D (max deviation 0.0049). Includes the lineage theorem
  (complex re-read erase == delta-rule beta=1), the LMS stability condition
  for corrective writes, and a matched-budget comparison against delta-rule
  and attention operators with an honest (unrounded) almost-equivalence TOST.
  Code, trained checkpoints, experiment logs and a verification report are
  included.
